---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About The Project — The Headless Journal"
  description="Learn about The Headless Journal, a reference demonstration of modern headless WordPress paired with Astro static site generation."
>
  <div class="py-8 sm:py-12 lg:py-16">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 space-y-12">
      <!-- Breadcrumb -->
      <nav class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-semibold text-stone-500" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/" class="hover:text-stone-900 transition-colors">Home</a>
        <span>/</span>
        <span class="text-stone-900">About</span>
      </nav>

      <!-- Page Header -->
      <header class="border-b border-stone-200 pb-8">
        <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-indigo-700">Project Overview</span>
        <h1 class="font-editorial-serif text-3xl sm:text-4xl md:text-5xl font-extrabold text-stone-900 tracking-tight mt-2">
          About The Headless Journal
        </h1>
        <p class="font-editorial-serif italic text-lg sm:text-xl text-stone-600 mt-4 leading-relaxed">
          A real-world engineering demonstration showing how WordPress can be leveraged as a modern headless CMS with Astro.
        </p>
      </header>

      <!-- Main Prose Content -->
      <div class="article-prose space-y-6">
        <p class="lead">
          <strong>The Headless Journal</strong> is an open-source technical starter and showcase.
          Its purpose is to provide software engineers and editorial teams with an un-opinionated,
          battle-tested blueprint for decoupling WordPress into a lightning-fast static publication powered by Astro.
        </p>

        <h2>The Publishing Dilemma</h2>
        <p>
          For over two decades, editorial teams have relied on WordPress for authoring, editing, and publishing.
          However, modern frontend expectations demand sub-second page loads, near-perfect Core Web Vitals, and bulletproof
          security.
        </p>
        <p>
          Monolithic PHP themes frequently struggle under viral traffic and require continuous server tuning.
          By contrast, modern static site generators render every article into pure HTML ahead of time, serving content directly
          from global edge CDNs with zero runtime server latency.
        </p>

        <h2>Why Astro?</h2>
        <p>
          Astro was chosen as the frontend framework because of its foundational <strong>Islands Architecture</strong> and
          <strong>Zero-JS by default</strong> philosophy. Unlike React-heavy SPAs that download megabytes of hydration code
          simply to display static typography, Astro compiles components down to raw, semantic HTML.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Sub-100ms TTFB:</strong> Edge-cached static HTML serves almost instantaneously.</li>
          <li><strong>Perfect Accessibility &amp; SEO:</strong> Search crawlers and assistive technologies receive pure semantic DOM trees.</li>
          <li><strong>Developer Ergonomics:</strong> Component authoring with TypeScript and scoped styling without client-side bundle penalties.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Three-Tier Content Architecture</h2>
        <p>
          This demonstration project is designed around an extensible <strong>Adapter Pattern</strong> supporting three distinct execution modes:
        </p>

        <div class="not-prose my-8 space-y-4">
          <!-- Demo Mode Card -->
          <div class="p-5 bg-white border border-stone-200 rounded-xl shadow-xs">
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-stone-900 text-base">1. Demo Mode (Active)</h3>
              <span class="px-2.5 py-0.5 rounded text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-800">
                Functional Now
              </span>
            </div>
            <p class="text-stone-600 text-sm mt-2 leading-relaxed">
              Consumes local, structured JSON datasets with 8 comprehensive technical articles. Requires zero WordPress servers,
              databases, or external network calls. Allows developers to clone the repository and run the entire site locally in seconds.
            </p>
          </div>

          <!-- Free Mode Card -->
          <div class="p-5 bg-white border border-stone-200 rounded-xl shadow-xs">
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-stone-900 text-base">2. Free Mode (Active)</h3>
              <span class="px-2.5 py-0.5 rounded text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-800">
                Functional Now
              </span>
            </div>
            <p class="text-stone-600 text-sm mt-2 leading-relaxed">
              Connects directly to WordPress using the <strong>RKX API Studio Free</strong> plugin, delivering curated
              REST API responses (<code>/wp-json/rkx-api-studio/v1/posts</code>, <code>/categories</code>, <code>/featured</code>) mapped directly to the frontend's TypeScript content model.
            </p>
          </div>

          <!-- Pro Mode Card -->
          <div class="p-5 bg-white border border-stone-200 rounded-xl shadow-xs">
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-stone-900 text-base">3. Pro Mode (Active)</h3>
              <span class="px-2.5 py-0.5 rounded text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider bg-indigo-100 text-indigo-800">
                Functional Now
              </span>
            </div>
            <p class="text-stone-600 text-sm mt-2 leading-relaxed">
              Expands capabilities with <strong>RKX API Studio Pro</strong>, unlocking the <strong>Dynamic Route Builder</strong>
              (<code>/wp-json/rkx/v1/posts/&#123;slug&#125;</code>, <code>/post-ids/&#123;id&#125;</code>, <code>/categories/&#123;slug&#125;</code>)
              under a configured Pro custom REST namespace (<code>rkx/v1</code>, replacing the default <code>rkx-api-studio/v1</code> namespace),
              typed ACF field normalization, and server-side Bearer authentication.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <h2>RKX API Studio Integration</h2>
        <p>
          The middle layer between WordPress and Astro is managed by <strong>RKX API Studio</strong>, developed by
          <a href="https://rkxbeta.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-indigo-600 font-semibold hover:underline">RKXBeta</a>.
          Instead of forcing frontend engineers to wrestle with default, verbose WordPress REST responses, the API Studio provides clean,
          structured endpoints tailored for static site generation and modern frontend consumption.
        </p>

        <blockquote>
          <p>“Clean data contracts turn WordPress into a joy to consume for modern frontend engineers.”</p>
        </blockquote>

        <h2>Open Source &amp; Extensibility</h2>
        <p>
          The codebase is intentionally clean, documented, and free of proprietary lock-in. Developers are encouraged
          to inspect the adapter pattern in <code>src/lib/content.ts</code> and adapt it for their own publishing workflows.
        </p>
      </div>

        <!-- Action Footer -->
      <div class="pt-8 border-t border-stone-200 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-4">
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
          <a
            href="/blog"
            class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-5 py-2.5 rounded-lg text-sm font-semibold bg-stone-900 text-white hover:bg-stone-800 transition-colors shadow-xs"
          >
            <span>Explore The Articles</span>
            <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M14 5l7 7m0 0l-7 7m7-7H3" />
            </svg>
          </a>
        </div>

        <a
          href="https://github.com/rkxbeta/headless-wordpress-astro-demo"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs font-semibold text-stone-600 hover:text-indigo-600 transition-colors"
        >
          <span>View on GitHub</span>
          <svg class="w-3.5 h-3.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M10 6H6a2 2 0 00-2 2v10a2 2 0 002 2h10a2 2 0 002-2v-4M14 4h6m0 0v6m0-6L10 14" />
          </svg>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
